B.a7u=new A.e("What is the gold standard for diagnosing facet (zygapophyseal) joint pain?",B.Xh,2,"The double diagnostic block is the gold standard. Two separate blocks with different anesthetics are performed; if the patient gets >80% relief both times with duration matching the drug used, the diagnosis is confirmed. MRI findings correlate poorly with pain.")
B.WF=s(["Warmth, redness, and swelling","A palpable taut band, referred pain pattern, and local twitch response (jump sign)","Crepitus, locking, and catching","Numbness, tingling, and weakness"],t.s)
B.a4e=new A.e("What are the three pathognomonic features of a myofascial trigger point?",B.WF,1,"A trigger point has: (1) a palpable taut band, (2) referred pain to a distant area when pressed, and (3) a local twitch response (jump sign) when the band is snapped. This distinguishes it from a simple tender point.")
