B.Iq=new A.a6("Musculoskeletal: Wrist",B.Ng)
B.S0=s(["Level 5 - Supervision","Level 6 - Modified Independence","Level 7 - Complete Independence","Level 4 - Minimal Assist"],t.s)
B.a3k=new A.e("On the Functional Independence Measure, what is the minimum level at which no physical helper is required?",B.S0,1,"Level 6 (Modified Independence) and Level 7 (Complete Independence) both require no helper to be physically present. Level 6 allows use of a device or extra time.")
B.Xp=s(["Level 2 - Maximal Assist","Level 1 - Total Assist","Level 3 - Moderate Assist","Level 4 - Minimal Assist"],t.s)
B.a61=new A.e("On the FIM scale, a task that requires two helpers is automatically scored as which level?",B.Xp,1,"If a task requires two helpers for any reason, it is automatically scored as Level 1 (Total Assist) regardless of how much effort the patient contributes.")
B.Ux=s(["Greater than 10 mmHg","Greater than 15 mmHg","Greater than 20 mmHg","Greater than 25 mmHg"],t.s)
B.aaf=new A.e("What is the ICP threshold at which treatment intervention is required?",B.Ux,2,"The threshold for ICP intervention is greater than 20 mmHg. If ICP stays above 20 for more than five minutes, action must be taken.")
B.UQ=s(["Greater than 40 mmHg","Greater than 50 mmHg","Greater than 60 mmHg","Greater than 70 mmHg"],t.s)
B.a7V=new A.e("In the CPP equation (CPP = MAP - ICP), what is the minimum target cerebral perfusion pressure?",B.UQ,2,"The target CPP is greater than 60 mmHg. Data shows that if CPP drops below 50, mortality increases significantly.")
B.Xv=s(["It is cheaper and more widely available","It has a shorter half-life allowing wake-up tests and it lowers ICP","It raises blood pressure which improves cerebral perfusion","It has no significant side effects in TBI patients"],t.s)
B.a6_=new A.e("Why is propofol preferred over benzodiazepines for sedation in the neuro ICU for TBI patients?",B.Xv,1,"Propofol has a very short half-life allowing wake-up tests within minutes, and it also directly lowers ICP. Benzodiazepines have long half-lives that obscure neurological exams.")
B.R7=s([B.a3k,B.a61,B.aaf,B.a7V,B.a6_],t.b)
B.Ir=new A.a6("Traumatic Brain Injury 3",B.R7)
B.Sl=s(["Threshold devices are cheaper","Threshold devices produce resistance independent of flow rate, preventing cheating","Flow-dependent devices are more consistent","Threshold devices are only for COPD"],t.s)
B.a52=new A.e("What distinguishes a threshold loading device from a flow-dependent device for inspiratory muscle training?",B.Sl,1,"Threshold loading requires a predetermined mouth pressure to open a valve regardless of flow rate, so patients cannot cheat by breathing slowly.")
B.OH=s(["Too noisy for sleep","Negative pressure sucks the upper airway closed, causing severe apnea","Cannot generate enough pressure for obesity","Interferes with CPAP"],t.s)
B.a6Q=new A.e("Why is the iron lung contraindicated in obstructive sleep apnea patients?",B.OH,1,"Negative pressure creates suction that pulls the tongue and soft tissues closed in OSA patients, actively suffocating them each cycle.")
B.Wi=s(["Severe COPD","An inflated cuff","Thick secretions","Age over 80"],t.s)
B.a9v=new A.e("What is the absolute contraindication for a Passy-Muir speaking valve on a tracheostomy patient?",B.Wi,1,"With inflated cuff + one-way valve, air enters but cannot exit \u2014 causing breath stacking, barotrauma, or cardiac arrest.")
B.ZO=s(["100 bpm","110 bpm","120 bpm","140 bpm"],t.s)
B.a8D=new A.e("At what heart rate should exercise be stopped during pulmonary rehabilitation?",B.ZO,2,"If heart rate goes over 120 bpm during pulmonary rehab, hold exercise.")
B.Yn=s(["15 degrees","30 degrees","45 degrees","60 degrees"],t.s)
B.a6T=new A.e("What is the minimum angle a patient must be seated at for the pneumobelt to function?",B.Yn,1,"The pneumobelt relies on gravity, so the patient must be >30 degrees upright (75 degrees optimal). It cannot work lying flat.")
B.V0=s([B.a52,B.a6Q,B.a9v,B.a8D,B.a6T],t.b)
