B.a70=new A.e("What is the classic radiographic finding of psoriatic arthritis that distinguishes it from RA?",B.Za,1,"The pencil-in-cup deformity is a signature radiographic finding of psoriatic arthritis, where the distal phalanx erodes to a point (pencil) sitting in the widened base of the adjacent phalanx (cup).")
B.Nh=s(["They cause liver failure in HIV patients","They severely tank CD4 counts and can trigger opportunistic infections or Kaposi sarcoma","They interact with antiretroviral medications","They cause severe skin reactions in HIV"],t.s)
B.a3m=new A.e("Why are methotrexate and oral corticosteroids contraindicated in HIV-positive patients with psoriatic arthritis?",B.Nh,1,"Methotrexate is a potent immunosuppressant that can severely reduce CD4 counts, leading to opportunistic infections. Oral steroids can also tank immunity and trigger Kaposi sarcoma flares in HIV patients.")
B.X6=s(["Low white blood cell count","Normal glucose level","Crystals present","Bloody fluid"],t.s)
B.a3P=new A.e("In reactive arthritis, what synovial fluid finding helps rule out septic arthritis?",B.X6,1,"In reactive arthritis, the joint itself is sterile (it is an immune reaction to a distant infection), so synovial fluid glucose remains normal. In septic arthritis, bacteria consume glucose, causing it to plummet.")
B.Wz=s(["Myositis","Malar rash that spares the nasolabial folds","Mucosal dryness","Meningitis"],t.s)
B.a80=new A.e("What is the DOPAMINE RASH mnemonic criterion 'M' for in SLE diagnosis?",B.Wz,1,"M stands for Malar rash, the classic butterfly rash across the cheeks and bridge of the nose. The critical detail is that it spares the nasolabial folds; if redness extends into those creases, consider rosacea instead.")
