B.a8W=new A.e("Central post-stroke pain (thalamic pain syndrome) is best treated initially with which class of medications?",B.ZC,2,"Central post-stroke pain (Dejerine-Roussy syndrome) is a neuropathic pain condition best treated with anticonvulsants (gabapentin, pregabalin) or tricyclic antidepressants (amitriptyline). It does not respond well to NSAIDs or opioids.")
