B.PS=s(["MS always presents before age 15","If a person migrates from a high-risk to low-risk area before age 15, they acquire the lower risk of their new location","MS symptoms must be present for 15 years before diagnosis","Disability becomes permanent after 15 years"],t.s)
B.a8w=new A.e("What is the 15-year rule in MS epidemiology?",B.PS,1,"If a person migrates from a high-risk to a low-risk area before age 15, they acquire the lower MS risk. Migration after age 15 retains the original high risk, suggesting environmental exposure during childhood sets the immunological thermostat.")
B.Wh=s(["HLA-B27","HLA-DRB1*1501 on chromosome 6","BRCA1","ApoE4"],t.s)
B.aa7=new A.e("What is the strongest genetic risk factor identified for MS?",B.Wh,1,"The HLA-DRB1*1501 allele on chromosome 6 is the strongest genetic risk factor for MS. It is involved in immune system antigen presentation, consistent with an autoimmune disease.")
B.QT=s(["3-5%","15%","39%","75%"],t.s)
B.a4X=new A.e("What is the concordance rate for MS in monozygotic (identical) twins?",B.QT,2,"The concordance rate is 39% in identical twins. This proves both genetic susceptibility (much higher than the 3-5% for fraternal twins) and environmental influence (if purely genetic, it would be 100%).")
B.Yq=s(["Relapse rates increase throughout pregnancy","Relapse rates decrease during pregnancy (especially third trimester) but spike in the first 3-6 months postpartum","Pregnancy has no effect on relapse rates","Relapse rates increase only in the first trimester"],t.s)
B.a8E=new A.e("How does pregnancy affect MS relapse rates?",B.Yq,1,"During pregnancy, the immune system shifts from pro-inflammatory TH1 to anti-inflammatory TH2, decreasing relapses. In the first 3-6 months postpartum, relapses spike as the immune system rebounds. Long-term prognosis is unchanged.")
